WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.434
-Welcome, welcome, welcome.
Welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.434 --> 00:00:06.367
You're here.
Thank you for watching.

00:00:06.367 --> 00:00:09.033
Thank you for being here.
This is very exciting.

00:00:09.033 --> 00:00:11.200
Tomorrow night's
Powerball jackpot

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.067
is one of the biggest in history
at $1.4 billion, by the way.

00:00:16.067 --> 00:00:18.634
Yeah.
Yeah, $1.4 billion,

00:00:18.634 --> 00:00:20.434
which is also the number
of couples dressing

00:00:20.434 --> 00:00:22.100
as Barbie and Ken for Halloween.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:25.100
"You're doing it, too.
I thought we were the only..."

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.467
[ Laughter ]
Did you guys see this?

00:00:27.467 --> 00:00:29.901
Here in New York City
for the second weekend in a row

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.868
there's a heavy chance of rain
and flash flooding.

00:00:32.868 --> 00:00:34.601
[ Audience groans ]

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:36.033
Honestly, when it comes
to getting flashed

00:00:36.033 --> 00:00:38.067
in New York City,
this is the best-case scenario.

00:00:38.067 --> 00:00:40.601
[ Laughter ]
I will say that.

00:00:40.601 --> 00:00:42.367
You can tell a storm is coming

00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:43.601
'cause this morning
on the way to work,

00:00:43.601 --> 00:00:46.000
I saw a rat with a beard
building a tiny ark.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.334
And I go, "That's usually
a sign that the storm's coming."

00:00:51.667 --> 00:00:54.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:56.300
I always go to the rats.
I go -- Yeah.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.667
So, movie news today.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:59.767
50 years after
the original film was released,

00:00:59.767 --> 00:01:02.734
"The Exorcist: Believer"
hit theaters.

00:01:02.734 --> 00:01:05.934
Yeah, so if you want to see
someone spit up pea soup,

00:01:05.934 --> 00:01:07.067
you can either watch
"The Exorcist"

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.434
or "The Golden Bachelor."

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.167
[ Laughter ]
It's up to you.

00:01:10.167 --> 00:01:13.300
"He's had enough.
He's full. Stop feeding him."

00:01:15.133 --> 00:01:16.734
Speaking of "The Golden
Bachelor," last night,

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.133
there was an all-new episode.

00:01:18.133 --> 00:01:19.667
And if you haven't seen it,
the show is pretty different

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:20.834
from the regular "Bachelor."

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.133
It's a great show,
but it's different.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:23.534
-Really?
-Yeah, well, like

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:24.801
on the regular "Bachelor,"

00:01:24.801 --> 00:01:27.167
the limo drops off
each contestant,

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:28.300
but on "The Golden Bachelor,"

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:30.501
the limo always has
its left turn signal on.

00:01:30.501 --> 00:01:31.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:31.701 --> 00:01:33.467
There's differences between --
Yeah.

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.601
-Yeah.

00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:36.868
[ Applause ]

00:01:36.868 --> 00:01:38.100
Let me give you another example.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.434
On the regular "Bachelor,"

00:01:39.434 --> 00:01:40.901
"I'm falling in love with you,"

00:01:40.901 --> 00:01:42.167
but on "The Golden Bachelor,"

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.200
"I've fallen in love with you

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:44.267
and I can't get up."

00:01:44.267 --> 00:01:45.934
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:49.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.067
Up next on "The Bachelor,"

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:53.868
everyone is too young
to be on "The Golden Bachelor,"

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.067
but on "The Golden Bachelor,"

00:01:55.067 --> 00:01:56.968
everyone is too young
to run for president.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:59.100
Yeah, not -- not quite yet.

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:01.801
It's very close.

00:02:01.801 --> 00:02:03.601
Next on "The Bachelor,"

00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:05.000
Jesse Palmer is the host,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:06.033
but on "The Golden Bachelor,"

00:02:06.033 --> 00:02:08.033
Jesse Palmer
is the emergency contact.

00:02:08.033 --> 00:02:11.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.734 --> 00:02:13.133
Next up on "The Bachelor,"

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:15.167
one-on-one date to go on a hike.
Ooh.

00:02:15.167 --> 00:02:16.934
On "The Golden Bachelor,"
one-on-one date

00:02:16.934 --> 00:02:19.033
to the Apple store
because Gerry somehow

00:02:19.033 --> 00:02:22.033
switched his iPhone
to Portuguese.

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:25.667
"I can't underst--"

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:29.133
Finally the regular "Bachelor,"
streaming on Hulu,

00:02:29.133 --> 00:02:31.767
but "The Golden Bachelor"
is streaming on Flomax.

00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:33.434
There you go.
The shows are different.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:34.667
The shows are different shows.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:38.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.801 --> 00:02:41.033
Well, switching gears,
according to a new report,

00:02:41.033 --> 00:02:42.534
right after he left office,

00:02:42.534 --> 00:02:45.300
former President Trump
shared classified information

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:48.801
about nuclear submarines
with an Australian businessman.

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:50.567
[ Audience "oohs" ]

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:52.534
But Trump denied it.
He was like, "That's impossible.

00:02:52.534 --> 00:02:54.167
I don't even
speak Australian."

00:02:54.167 --> 00:02:57.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.167 --> 00:03:00.667
Some business news.

00:03:00.667 --> 00:03:04.801
Crocs just announced that they
are releasing cowboy boots.

00:03:04.801 --> 00:03:08.100
This is real.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.367
Can we -- Can we see a photo
of these things?

00:03:10.367 --> 00:03:11.200
This is real.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.300
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:14.267
-Ooh-wee!

00:03:14.267 --> 00:03:17.400
-Oh.
-It's amazing.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.834
For the first time in one shoe,

00:03:18.834 --> 00:03:20.534
it is the good,
the bad, and the ugly.

00:03:20.534 --> 00:03:22.234
It's un--

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:24.000
It's hard to be taken seriously
as a cowboy.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:26.167
Every time you walk into a
saloon it sounds like this.

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:28.701
[ Shoes squeaking loudly ]

00:03:31.734 --> 00:03:34.400
Hey, I saw that Travis Kelce
said the NFL

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:35.901
might be going
a little overboard

00:03:35.901 --> 00:03:38.434
talking about his relationship
with Taylor Swift.

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:39.968
And I think the NFL
heard him,

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.534
because I just saw a promo
for Sunday's Chiefs game

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:44.901
and it seems like they're back
to focusing on football,

00:03:44.901 --> 00:03:46.067
not who's in the stands.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:47.667
Well, watch this.

00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:49.300
-This Sunday, Patrick Mahomes

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.934
and the defending Super Bowl
champion Kansas City Chiefs

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.968
head to Minneapolis
to take on Kirk Cousins

00:03:53.968 --> 00:03:56.801
and the Vikings --
kickoff at 4:25.

00:03:56.801 --> 00:03:58.901
-Yeah, I like that.
It's very professional.

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:01.834
-Yeah. That's very professional.
-And respectful. And --

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.267
Hold on.
I'm being told there's

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.033
a new promo out
for Sunday's game.

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:07.033
-Really?
-Let's take a look at this one.

00:04:07.033 --> 00:04:09.934
-This Sunday, it's Chiefs
at Vikings featuring Mahomes,

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.167
Cousins, Kelce,
and who knows who else?

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:13.868
We'll let you fill in
the blank space.

00:04:13.868 --> 00:04:16.133
[ Chuckles ]
Kickoff at 4:25.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.567
-Now, I can sort
of see a little bit --

00:04:18.567 --> 00:04:22.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
No, I mean, there's still...

00:04:22.734 --> 00:04:25.501
They teased it a little, but
it's still focused on football.

00:04:25.501 --> 00:04:27.067
You know, so that's so --
I'm sorry.

00:04:27.067 --> 00:04:30.834
I'm being told
there's another new promo.

00:04:30.834 --> 00:04:33.067
This is -- It's out right now.
It's fresh. Here it is.

00:04:33.067 --> 00:04:34.901
-Listen up, bitches!

00:04:34.901 --> 00:04:37.734
It's Chiefs versus
who the [bleep] cares?

00:04:37.734 --> 00:04:40.367
Tay Tay is gonna slay slay
all day day!

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:41.534
It'll be cray cray!

00:04:41.534 --> 00:04:43.667
Mahomes is going to wear
a friendship bracelet

00:04:43.667 --> 00:04:46.801
while he does his teddies to
Taylor's new bae bae, Tray Tray!

00:04:46.801 --> 00:04:48.701
But you won't even see the game.

00:04:48.701 --> 00:04:50.200
'cause we're keeping
the camera on Taylor

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:51.834
the whole [bleep] time!

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:53.534
The Chiefs
just scored a touchdown?

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:54.634
Who gives a [bleep]?!

00:04:54.634 --> 00:04:56.667
Mother just took a sip
from her drink!

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:58.801
-Hydrate!
-S-S-Slurp!

00:04:58.801 --> 00:05:01.634
She is our queen,
and we are her peasants!

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.100
Kickoff at 4:25.

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:09.367
-On NBC.

00:05:09.367 --> 00:05:12.133
On NBC this Sunday, yeah.

00:05:12.133 --> 00:05:14.234
Finally, this week,
the city of Indianapolis

00:05:14.234 --> 00:05:16.567
experienced an unusual problem.
Watch this.

00:05:16.567 --> 00:05:19.767
-People living in Indianapolis
are on monkey watch.

00:05:19.767 --> 00:05:22.567
Here's why. A pet monkey owned
by a private citizen escaped.

00:05:22.567 --> 00:05:25.968
-Some other neighbors had said
it bit a couple of people.

00:05:25.968 --> 00:05:28.000
Then I was outside,
and it ran up in my garage,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.367
pinned me against the door.

00:05:29.367 --> 00:05:32.267
-The monkey was last seen
in far east Indianapolis,

00:05:32.267 --> 00:05:33.968
drinking a beer
out of a trash can.

00:05:33.968 --> 00:05:38.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.267
-From the creators
of "Cocaine Bear" comes...

00:05:40.267 --> 00:05:42.801
[ Laughter ]
..."Beer Monkey"!

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:45.634
-Thank you.

00:05:45.634 --> 00:05:47.167
But, you know, today's Friday.

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:48.934
You know, let's kick off
the weekend with something fun.

00:05:48.934 --> 00:05:51.434
You know, let's -- let's
catch up on some e-mails.

00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:52.634
-Right.
-It's our first week back.

00:05:52.634 --> 00:05:53.601
-Yeah.
-You know,

00:05:53.601 --> 00:05:54.801
I want to thank everybody

00:05:54.801 --> 00:05:56.901
for what a great week
of shows we had here.

00:05:56.901 --> 00:05:58.234
-Grateful to be back.

00:05:58.234 --> 00:05:59.434
-Maybe I'll send out
some thank-you notes.

00:05:59.434 --> 00:06:00.567
-Really?
-If you guys --

00:06:00.567 --> 00:06:02.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:02.634 --> 00:06:06.033
Can do them right now? Do
you mind if I do it right now?

00:06:06.033 --> 00:06:08.434
Thank you so much.
-Wow.

00:06:08.434 --> 00:06:10.300
-James...can I get some

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:12.334
thank-you-note-writing music,
please?

00:06:12.334 --> 00:06:14.100
[ Somber music playing ]
Wow.

00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:15.601
-Wow. He's happy to be back.

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.200
-A little rusty.
He's a little rusty.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.801 --> 00:06:21.000
-Meep!

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.534
♪♪

00:06:24.534 --> 00:06:26.901
-Thank you, Bed Bath $ Beyond,

00:06:26.901 --> 00:06:29.334
for dressing up
as Spirit Halloween this year.

00:06:29.334 --> 00:06:31.501
[ Laughter ]

00:06:31.501 --> 00:06:33.167
[ Applause ]

00:06:33.167 --> 00:06:35.968
-[ Chuckles ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:35.968 --> 00:06:37.267
-Oh, it's beyond.

00:06:37.267 --> 00:06:38.434
♪♪

00:06:38.434 --> 00:06:41.234
-Thank you, Las Vegas Sphere,

00:06:41.234 --> 00:06:43.934
for looking like Epcot
going through an emo phase.

00:06:43.934 --> 00:06:45.968
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:06:45.968 --> 00:06:48.634
Don't talk to me!

00:06:48.634 --> 00:06:50.234
You're not my real dad!

00:06:50.234 --> 00:06:52.033
[ Laughter ]

00:06:52.033 --> 00:06:54.267
-[ Laughs ]

00:06:54.267 --> 00:06:55.634
♪♪

00:06:55.634 --> 00:06:58.000
-Thank you, TSA body scanners,

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.434
for making me feel like
I can't get on the plane

00:07:00.434 --> 00:07:02.801
unless I do the "M" in "YMCA."

00:07:02.801 --> 00:07:04.634
[ Applause ]

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.501
-Pat down.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:11.934
♪♪

00:07:11.934 --> 00:07:13.868
-Thank you, fish sticks,

00:07:13.868 --> 00:07:16.400
for being perfect for anyone
who ate a mozzarella stick

00:07:16.400 --> 00:07:18.934
and thought, "If only
this tasted like carp."

00:07:18.934 --> 00:07:21.067
[ Laughter ]

00:07:21.067 --> 00:07:23.567
[ Applause ]

00:07:23.567 --> 00:07:24.801
♪ I can dream ♪

00:07:24.801 --> 00:07:27.167
♪ Can't I dream? ♪

00:07:29.501 --> 00:07:30.701
♪♪

00:07:30.701 --> 00:07:32.901
Thank you, clear umbrellas,

00:07:32.901 --> 00:07:35.767
for pranking the rain
into thinking it's gonna get me.

00:07:35.767 --> 00:07:39.667
[ Laughter,
cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.667 --> 00:07:42.033
[ Indistinct ]

00:07:44.033 --> 00:07:46.000
-Whew! [ Indistinct ]

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.968
-[ Laughs ]
-Hoo! [ Laughs ]

00:07:48.968 --> 00:07:50.200
-Alright.

00:07:51.267 --> 00:07:52.601
♪♪

00:07:52.601 --> 00:07:53.634
Thank you,

00:07:53.634 --> 00:07:56.067
Hershey's Halloween
variety packs,

00:07:56.067 --> 00:07:58.367
for single-handedly
keeping Mr. Goodbar alive.

00:07:58.367 --> 00:08:00.501
-Aw.
[ Applause ]

00:08:00.501 --> 00:08:02.133
-What? What? what?
-Come on!

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:04.167
I'm looking for Mr. Goodbar!

00:08:04.167 --> 00:08:05.334
-I don't see it much.

00:08:07.067 --> 00:08:08.801
♪♪

00:08:08.801 --> 00:08:11.400
Thank you, trying to help
my children with their homework,

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.601
for being
a tough but fair reminder

00:08:13.601 --> 00:08:15.100
of why I got into comedy.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:17.300
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

